WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:03.630
- [Narrator] The Gaza Strip
is a densely populated area

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.450
with more than 2 million
residents stretching

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.290
for 25 miles between Israel and Egypt.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.960
But just underneath this
sprawling landscape,

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.730
another layer exists, a
vast labyrinth of tunnels.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.060
The underground maze was
largely built by Hamas.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.750
The group designated by the
US as a terrorist organization

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.540
controls the Palestinian enclave.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.600
As Israel prepares for a
potential ground defensive

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.060
in the territory following a broad assault

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.860
by Hamas on October 7th,

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.070
the subterranean network
could play a key role.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.980
So here's why experts say
these tunnels could make

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.640
urban combats costly for
both Israeli soldiers

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.953
and Palestinian civilians.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:52.713
The underground network has
existed for decades inside Gaza.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.480
Previously it was largely used
as a roots to smuggle goods

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.020
and weapons from Egypt into
the narrowest strip of land

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.573
that's twice the size of Washington DC.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.540
But since then, the tunnels have evolved

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.360
to become a key military asset for Hamas.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.360
- I went in 2014 with the
IDF into a Hamas built tunnel

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.210
during the conflict at that time,

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.400
and it was a pretty crazy
experience in a sense.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.610
These were pretty sophisticated tunnels.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.730
I'm about six foot, and
they were, you know,

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.980
I didn't have to bend down at all in them.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.890
They were very well
reinforced with concrete.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.820
There was communications
lines running down the side

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.030
of them, and then they also
had like, almost like a sort

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:42.840
of little rails or like a
sort of railway line running

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.150
along the length of the tunnel.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:49.080
- [Narrator] During Israel's
seven week war on Gaza in 2014,

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.550
the Israel defense forces

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.115
or IDF said it destroyed 32 tunnels.

00:01:54.115 --> 00:01:56.730
(bomb exploding)

00:01:56.730 --> 00:02:00.540
They were used to hide
weapons, equipments and troops,

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.430
but also allowed Hamas militants

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.380
to launch surprise attacks

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:07.050
using cross-border underground networks.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:10.590
In the years since then,
Hamas has continued

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.960
to develop its tunnel infrastructure,

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.333
and Israel has continued to target it.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:20.010
This map, based on a
graphic shared by the IDF

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:24.153
represents networks of tunnels
that Israel said it damaged.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.040
- I think the expectation is that there is

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.040
still a significant subterranean network

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.440
that Israel's gonna encounter if

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:37.200
and when it goes in into Gaza this time.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.420
- [Narrator] Former Israeli
security officials say

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.030
Hamas has built hundreds of miles

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:45.063
of underground tunnels
in the last year or more.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.920
Israel readying for a possible
ground invasion of Gaza

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.540
by carrying out airstrikes

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.450
targeting the subterranean network.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.750
- I think that the Israeli,
the strategy will be to try

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.230
to destroy as much of the
tunnel network as possible

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.930
before they launch a ground invasion.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.280
- [Narrator] However, the operation

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.180
to destroy them could be
challenging for Israeli forces.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.973
One of the biggest
issues is locating them.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:16.380
- Gaza is a dense urban environment

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.450
and being able to discern precisely

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.110
where a continuous tunnel,

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:26.130
which may in fact be deep
underground is located

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:30.390
as opposed to possibly natural pockets

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.810
of slightly differing geology,

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:37.950
or a host of other aspects
of the built up environment,

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.350
that's a really hard challenge.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.810
- [Narrator] Even if a tunnel is located,

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:45.780
additional factors
including its depth can mean

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.660
precision bombs can
struggle to destroy it.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.360
- It depends not only on knowing precisely

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.820
where the tunnel is beneath the surface,

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:58.290
but on having the
explosive power to be able

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:02.910
to damage a tunnel network that's beneath

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:06.990
perhaps layers of concrete,
possibly layers of metal,

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:10.410
whatever the built up
environment entails inherently,

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:13.740
as well as whatever materials
have gone into construction

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:15.360
of the tunnel itself.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.560
And the net result is that tunnels are

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:24.560
relatively invulnerable in
many cases to air attack.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.180
- [Narrator] And let's
say any Israeli operation

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:30.630
to destroy the Gaza tunnel
system could be complicated

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:32.523
by the presence of hostages.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:36.480
Hamas' armed wing said in
the statements on Telegram

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:38.220
that some of them were being held

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.230
in the underground tunnels.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:43.440
- If the aim is to rescue hostages,

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.600
they can't be detonating explosives

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:49.440
within the tunnel complex, which
might kill everyone inside.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:52.830
It's going to require ground forces,

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:55.470
specifically tunneling forces who know how

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:57.300
to operate in these tight spaces,

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.190
who have trained extensively

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:03.270
in how to minimize the risk of ambushes

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:07.653
and how to avoid triggering
various booby traps.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:11.490
- [Narrator] One 85-year-old
hostage who was released

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:14.073
by Hamas said she had been inside.

00:05:15.028 --> 00:05:18.527
- There are a huge, huge network

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:24.450
of tunnels underneath, it
looks like a spider web.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.970
- [Narrator] Entrances to the
subterranean passageways can

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:30.360
also be hidden within
residential infrastructure.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.390
Experts say as a war continues any mission

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:37.623
to target the tunnels also
brings risks to civilians.

